# Per-checkout sync state, not project source. All three are written by the
# sync tooling and address entities in one specific org and project, so a
# committed copy would point every checkout at ours. A fresh checkout has no
# baseline — establish one against your own project with an explicit
# --org/--project on the first pull.
.metabind/state.json
metabind.resolved

# Secret VALUES are KMS-encrypted server-side and never sync. Never commit a
# value. `.metabind/secrets.json` holds only the secret NAMES this project
# reads, and it is what `metabind inspect` reports as the consent preview, so
# it is committed on purpose — without it `inspect` under-reports what
# `install --yes` is agreeing to.

.DS_Store
node_modules/
